    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="412bb3fc-8466-5de6-854d-3085a7c2166e" activityNameId="7b65be2f-8783-581d-ba08-40c46f9ae02d" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Mounting, through-hole technology, Pb-free solder</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Mounting, through-hole technology, Pb-free solder
Data are based on literature (report from a European research project in the field of lead-free soldering). Infrastructure and transportation efforts are based on own assumptions.; UUID: db859e65-1929-321b-9247-3bf5faea26d5
This dataset includes soldering material input, energy consumption and waste, as well as an estimation of emissions to air, the efforts for transportation and of the infrastructure for the mounting process of through-hole components. Input of PWB and components are not included in this dataset.
Location: Data from a European study- representing global valuable values for the mounting activities in the electronics industry. Besides globalized production at the inventory level, the energy consumption is expected to decrease by 17% according to literature.
Technology: Information from two global electronics producing companies in the framework of a European study.
Time period: Unspecified
Production volume: 
Sampling: own estimation
Extrapolations: see Geography &amp; Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_db859e65-1929-321b-9247-3bf5faea26d5.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
